@startuml arch_session
!include palette.iuml
hide footbox
title What does an agent session load, and when?

actor User as user
participant "Tool\n(harness)" as tool
participant "Hooks" as hooks
participant "Model" as model
collections "Instructions" as rules
collections "Skills" as skills
participant "Subagent" as sub

== Session start ==
tool -> rules : global rules\n(&#126;/.agents/AGENTS.md)
tool -> rules : the project's AGENTS.md
tool -> skills : name and description\nof every skill
tool -> model : all of it, as context
opt Claude Code, after a compaction or resume
  tool -> hooks : session_refresh.py
  hooks --> tool : reminder, git state,\nnewest task notes
  tool -> model : added to the context
end

== A request ==
user -> tool : request or /name
tool -> model : the request
model -> skills : body of the matching\nSKILL.md
opt Claude Code, a file that matches a path rule
  tool -> model : dotagents-<skill>.md:\nuse that skill
end
model -> sub : delegate: scout,\ngate-runner or reviewer
note right of sub : fresh context, its own\ninstructions and tools
sub --> model : brief, gate table\nor findings

== Each tool call ==
model -> tool : shell command
tool -> hooks : before it: guard_bash.py
hooks --> tool : allow, or block\nwith the reason
opt Claude Code, the command failed
  tool -> hooks : repeated_failure.py
  hooks --> tool : on the third identical\nfailure: change approach
end
model -> tool : file edit
tool -> hooks : after it: after_edit.py
hooks --> tool : dash or syntax report,\nformat notice
tool --> model : results, reasons\nand notices

== End of the turn ==
model -> tool : done
opt Claude Code and Codex
  tool -> hooks : progress_check.py
  hooks --> tool : once, if the progress log\nmisses a commit: update it
end

legend right
  Solid arrow: a read or a call
  Dashed arrow: the reply
endlegend
@enduml
